QUICK REVISION
================================================================================

+---------------+-----------------------------------+
| Key Type      | Purpose                           |
+---------------+-----------------------------------+
| Primary Key   | Unique identification             |
| Foreign Key   | Table relationship                |
| Candidate Key | Possible primary key              |
| Super Key     | Unique combination                |
| Alternate Key | Unselected candidate key          |
| Composite Key | Multiple-column key               |
+---------------+-----------------------------------+

Memory Trick:
  Primary   → Main Key
  Foreign   → Reference Key
  Candidate → Possible Key
  Alternate → Remaining Key
  Composite → Combined Key

================================================================================
INTERVIEW POINTS
================================================================================

1. Primary key uniquely identifies rows.
2. Foreign key creates table relationships.
3. Candidate keys are possible primary keys.
4. Alternate key is unused candidate key.
5. Composite key uses multiple columns.
6. Super key uniquely identifies rows.
7. Primary key cannot contain NULL values.
